WEBVTT

00:00:02.910 --> 00:00:05.970
It was an era when a man lived as a warrior...

00:00:06.110 --> 00:00:10.780
He fought, staking his life on
his faith in the sword...

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:14.610
The final era... the Bakumatsu.

00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:29.000
Intrigue in the Bakumatsu

00:00:43.220 --> 00:00:46.850
On the land with the frozen moonlight

00:00:46.850 --> 00:00:50.690
It's rolling and drawing the line

00:00:50.690 --> 00:00:57.900
The era of destruction and rebirth now begins

00:00:57.900 --> 00:01:01.570
Heavily holding the freedom

00:01:01.570 --> 00:01:05.170
Choosing the invisible path

00:01:05.170 --> 00:01:12.240
Passing the sunset that's brighter than the daylight

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:19.250
The vessel of time moves on as if telling the dream

00:01:19.250 --> 00:01:28.350
There's a new dawn beyond the dark path

00:01:29.130 --> 00:01:36.270
We may have been born from the arm of darkness

00:01:36.270 --> 00:01:39.810
Just like being in an impossible love

00:01:39.810 --> 00:01:43.780
We wander into the light

00:01:43.780 --> 00:01:49.050
The path stretches indefinitely

00:01:49.050 --> 00:01:54.490
And there's no way to go back

00:02:22.610 --> 00:02:25.280
It is the eighth month of Keio 4.

00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:29.380
Ten days have passed since Edo
is renamed Tokyo.

00:02:31.460 --> 00:02:34.620
Edo Port

00:02:34.790 --> 00:02:36.760
Watch your step.

00:02:36.860 --> 00:02:38.260
We've got cold barley tea!

00:02:39.830 --> 00:02:42.230
Tea and sweet dumplings! Come see us!

00:02:42.230 --> 00:02:45.270
Who needs a rickshaw? Rickshaw!

00:02:45.270 --> 00:02:46.970
Now that we're here...

00:02:46.970 --> 00:02:49.440
Where should we go?

00:02:49.670 --> 00:02:52.240
Let's just head to the castle town for now.

00:02:52.240 --> 00:02:53.800
I've been waiting for you!

00:02:54.980 --> 00:02:55.950
Why?

00:02:57.620 --> 00:03:00.050
This is a very nice way to be greeted!

00:03:00.050 --> 00:03:00.950
Tayu?

00:03:01.250 --> 00:03:02.520
Hold my stuff.

00:03:04.360 --> 00:03:06.320
This is no coincidence, is it?

00:03:06.830 --> 00:03:08.120
Tayu!

00:03:08.230 --> 00:03:09.960
Don't you have to be at the shop?

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:11.530
I'm taking a break from it for a while.

00:03:11.530 --> 00:03:16.070
You didn't have to go out of your way
to do this for me!

00:03:16.070 --> 00:03:19.040
How could I say no
when So-san asks me a favor?

00:03:19.540 --> 00:03:20.910
So-san?

00:03:20.910 --> 00:03:23.470
Now I'm going to help you guys out, too.

00:03:23.710 --> 00:03:26.610
So I thank you for your support in advance.

00:03:26.950 --> 00:03:29.140
This is Tatsugoro Shinmon.

00:03:29.510 --> 00:03:36.220
I'm Tatsugoro. I got to see you
perform in Yokohama.

00:03:36.220 --> 00:03:38.310
I wish to make your acquaintance.

00:03:41.390 --> 00:03:46.660
Could you be the famous firefighter chief?

00:03:47.670 --> 00:03:51.760
Obviously my name has grown legs
and wandered around on its own.

00:03:52.540 --> 00:03:58.200
I've arranged the theater for you.
Don't worry about anything.

00:04:00.110 --> 00:04:02.810
Thank you very much for everything!

00:04:05.950 --> 00:04:08.320
Where's the master right now?

00:04:08.320 --> 00:04:11.720
Actually, even I don't know.

00:04:11.920 --> 00:04:16.880
All of a sudden I received a letter from him,
asking me to help you guys out.

00:04:17.730 --> 00:04:18.920
That's all.

00:04:19.060 --> 00:04:21.590
Hey, are you sure everything's going to be okay?

00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:25.700
He sent us the books,
but it's only half of the story.

00:04:25.800 --> 00:04:29.240
You worrying about it won't open the stage.

00:04:29.240 --> 00:04:32.300
It's the master we're talking about.
I'm sure he'll pop up before we know it.

00:04:32.440 --> 00:04:33.930
You don't get it, do you?

00:04:34.180 --> 00:04:36.700
If that happens Akizuki, too, will...

00:04:37.520 --> 00:04:40.880
He's after what the master took, right?

00:04:41.150 --> 00:04:42.820
The Head of the Conqueror...

00:04:42.820 --> 00:04:46.120
Right, and it's not going to be nice.

00:04:47.760 --> 00:04:55.720
To tell you the truth I'm scared of the next time
those two meet each other...

00:05:11.580 --> 00:05:14.020
Shinagawa

00:05:12.180 --> 00:05:14.280
Pick up two of them at a time.

00:05:22.090 --> 00:05:27.220
Wait just a little longer. We'll be done
once we place the ceiling.

00:05:28.900 --> 00:05:30.160
Everyone!

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:31.330
Great job!

00:05:31.600 --> 00:05:33.340
Why don't you take a break?

00:05:33.340 --> 00:05:34.370
Take a break!

00:05:34.370 --> 00:05:35.500
We have tea!

00:05:40.480 --> 00:05:41.710
A war, huh?

00:05:42.150 --> 00:05:45.180
Damn, it's a big mess.

00:05:45.180 --> 00:05:49.050
Supposedly things have gotten
very ugly in the north.

00:05:46.320 --> 00:05:49.050
Flagship Kaiyomaru

00:05:49.420 --> 00:05:53.690
Everyone's been saying that those ships
are going to head there sooner or later.

00:05:49.620 --> 00:05:55.120
Former Shogunate Fleet

00:05:55.260 --> 00:05:59.890
That's terrible. I'm just glad
that I wasn't born a samurai.

00:06:00.030 --> 00:06:01.520
It doesn't matter.

00:06:02.970 --> 00:06:06.170
Once a war starts, it doesn't matter
whether you're samurai or civilian.

00:06:06.170 --> 00:06:08.070
I know that much!

00:06:08.570 --> 00:06:11.340
That's why I became an actor.

00:06:12.440 --> 00:06:15.540
Killing and fighting on stage is enough for me.

00:06:15.710 --> 00:06:17.340
I agree.

00:06:17.820 --> 00:06:21.010
Hey, let's start!

00:06:31.900 --> 00:06:33.520
I've been waiting for you.

00:06:34.030 --> 00:06:36.700
Welcome to my Kaiyo!

00:06:34.030 --> 00:06:39.070
Takeaki Enomoto

00:06:37.370 --> 00:06:38.770
This is magnificent.

00:06:39.900 --> 00:06:42.910
It's obvious that it was build in Holland.

00:06:42.910 --> 00:06:49.310
I'm impressed, Mr. Ibaragi. You do have very
sharp insight just as the rumors say.

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:59.650
Please use this opportunity and join me
to rebuild the Tokugawa Family.

00:06:59.690 --> 00:07:02.090
Kaishu Katsu's Resident in Hikawa-cho, Akasaka

00:07:04.300 --> 00:07:06.930
So he still doesn't want to, huh?

00:07:06.930 --> 00:07:10.160
That Kamajiro... I guess he's after the money.

00:07:13.040 --> 00:07:19.580
Oh well, considering the size of his fleet, people
will notice if it moves no matter how slightly.

00:07:19.580 --> 00:07:22.240
And we're talking about them going to Aizu...

00:07:22.810 --> 00:07:27.220
Around that time, Aizu and the
Ouuetsu Reppan Alliance

00:07:27.450 --> 00:07:30.960
was on the verge of collapse due to
the attack by the new government,

00:07:27.840 --> 00:07:31.360
Month 5: Shirakawa Castle Falls

00:07:28.590 --> 00:07:31.360
Month 5: Nagaoka Castle Falls

00:07:31.160 --> 00:07:33.630
the Satsuma-Choshu Alliance.

00:07:32.090 --> 00:07:36.490
Month 6: Hirakata Port Stolen

00:07:32.860 --> 00:07:36.490
Month 6: Izumi Castle Falls

00:07:33.590 --> 00:07:36.490
Month 6: Yunagaya Castle Falls

00:07:33.630 --> 00:07:35.360
the Satsuma-Choshu Alliance.

00:07:35.360 --> 00:07:40.970
During that time, despite multiple requests
for aid, Enomoto refused to move.

00:07:37.100 --> 00:07:41.130
Month 7: Taira Castle Falls

00:07:37.850 --> 00:07:41.130
Month 7: Shibata Province Surrenders

00:07:38.600 --> 00:07:41.130
Month 7: Miharu Province defects

00:07:40.370 --> 00:07:41.130
Month 7: Souma Province vows allegiance

00:07:41.130 --> 00:07:42.300
Month 7: Nihonmatsu Castle Falls

00:07:41.800 --> 00:07:44.630
This was because he lacked sufficient war funds.

00:07:45.070 --> 00:07:50.800
At any rate, you don't know
what's going to happen in the war.

00:07:51.140 --> 00:07:54.150
Continue to keep an eye on him.

00:07:54.150 --> 00:07:54.840
Yes, sir.

00:08:05.520 --> 00:08:10.260
By the way Ibaragi-kun, there's a man
who came to visit me,

00:08:10.260 --> 00:08:13.560
and he told me that he's very much interested
in joining the meeting with you.

00:08:14.800 --> 00:08:15.990
Come in.

00:08:20.770 --> 00:08:23.940
I certainly suffered a defeat at that time.

00:08:24.210 --> 00:08:28.340
I already knew you weren't a man
who would die so easily.

00:08:30.010 --> 00:08:33.510
I also knew that you would show up here.

00:08:34.050 --> 00:08:36.820
Everything is going just as written in the script.

00:08:36.890 --> 00:08:42.850
My life and death simply depends on your script.
Is that what it is?

00:08:42.960 --> 00:08:48.630
I expect nothing less from today's
most popular writer, Sotetsu Ibaragi.

00:08:59.010 --> 00:09:00.270
This is good.

00:09:00.410 --> 00:09:02.010
That's Tatsugoro-san for you.

00:09:02.010 --> 00:09:03.110
Indeed.

00:09:03.110 --> 00:09:05.850
Hey, this is pretty nice!

00:09:05.850 --> 00:09:08.390
It's hard to believe this is something
that they just threw together.

00:09:08.390 --> 00:09:10.650
This is much better
than some random playhouse.

00:09:12.790 --> 00:09:14.690
There's a nice height, too.

00:09:15.360 --> 00:09:18.660
The sound of the audience's cheers
is coming back to me now.

00:09:20.230 --> 00:09:24.100
I've decided! I'm going to stake
my acting career on this performance!

00:09:24.100 --> 00:09:25.690
I've heard that before.

00:09:26.540 --> 00:09:29.510
Obviously the life that was supposedly
killed off gets resurrected.

00:09:29.510 --> 00:09:33.530
We'd better put our lives on the line
as long as it takes, too.

00:09:34.180 --> 00:09:35.810
Jubei Nakaiya...

00:09:36.050 --> 00:09:39.680
Damn... Who would've thought
that he was still alive...

00:09:40.080 --> 00:09:44.780
We can do a detailed cleaning later.
Let's start rehearsal.

00:09:49.830 --> 00:09:57.130
It looks like the Head doesn't want to
kill me off just yet, either.

00:09:57.440 --> 00:10:04.600
Giving people what they want
is what merchants do.

00:10:04.980 --> 00:10:09.680
I hope that you'll ask me for
anything you want, Enomoto-sama.

00:10:10.080 --> 00:10:12.420
That's great to hear.

00:10:12.420 --> 00:10:14.390
Now I can set sail.

00:10:14.390 --> 00:10:16.750
Let us show Katsu Awanokami
what we're made of!

00:10:37.540 --> 00:10:38.600
Fog?

00:10:53.660 --> 00:10:56.490
This thing is from that time...

00:11:03.870 --> 00:11:05.600
This is interesting.

00:11:06.040 --> 00:11:12.140
In the same way I play the role of myself,
everyone else plays themselves, too.

00:11:12.380 --> 00:11:13.480
It seems that way.

00:11:13.480 --> 00:11:15.170
That sounds like the master.

00:11:16.150 --> 00:11:17.440
So that means...

00:11:18.180 --> 00:11:21.810
Nakaiya himself is going to play his own role...

00:11:21.950 --> 00:11:23.110
That's interesting.

00:11:23.350 --> 00:11:25.950
Taking revenge on stage, huh?

00:11:27.290 --> 00:11:29.490
Hey, you're joking, right?

00:11:29.930 --> 00:11:33.530
First of all, how would we get him
on the stage in the first place?

00:11:33.530 --> 00:11:35.000
Good point.

00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:36.800
And, there's another thing.

00:11:37.570 --> 00:11:40.440
There's a role which no actor is assigned to.

00:11:41.710 --> 00:11:43.540
Is there another one?

00:11:44.280 --> 00:11:45.830
This must be it.

00:11:47.450 --> 00:11:50.420
Yes, the Eternal Assassin.

00:11:48.580 --> 00:11:51.140
<i>THE</i>
<i>ETERNAL</i>
<i>ASSASSIN</i>

00:11:54.190 --> 00:11:56.350
This is perfect.

00:11:59.620 --> 00:12:01.560
Time sure flies.

00:12:03.190 --> 00:12:04.530
Yes, it does.

00:12:04.530 --> 00:12:09.300
It's been almost three months
since we stopped hearing from Yojiro.

00:12:09.670 --> 00:12:11.470
Who knows where he is and what he's doing.

00:12:11.470 --> 00:12:13.440
That's not what I meant.

00:12:13.700 --> 00:12:16.760
I was talking about how long it's been
since the first time he came to this village.

00:12:17.380 --> 00:12:19.400
He was three or so.

00:12:19.710 --> 00:12:22.740
Remember we ate some udo tempura with him?

00:12:22.880 --> 00:12:23.940
That's right.

00:12:24.380 --> 00:12:26.440
He had such good eyes.

00:12:26.950 --> 00:12:29.390
"His eyes say that he knows his own destiny."

00:12:30.120 --> 00:12:32.460
I remember you said that once.

00:12:32.460 --> 00:12:34.190
Is that right?

00:12:35.290 --> 00:12:41.560
The Moontear Sword responded to Yojiro
and the Eternal Assassin was born.

00:12:43.070 --> 00:12:45.470
It is indeed destiny.

00:13:45.260 --> 00:13:47.600
Did it have something to do with the fog?

00:13:56.440 --> 00:13:59.480
Hurry, but be thorough. We must hurry!

00:13:59.480 --> 00:14:00.310
Yes, sir!

00:14:02.610 --> 00:14:06.780
We don't have time! Once you're finished
with your station, go help others!

00:14:06.950 --> 00:14:07.940
Yes, sir!

00:14:13.660 --> 00:14:16.860
Well, we've stayed too long.

00:14:17.130 --> 00:14:19.600
It looks like the departure is delayed.

00:14:20.160 --> 00:14:25.360
Kawai at Nagaoka is tired of waiting, too.
I'd like to take off immediately, but...

00:14:26.540 --> 00:14:29.800
At this rate the war will be over.

00:14:32.510 --> 00:14:33.840
It is the fifth month.

00:14:33.840 --> 00:14:36.870
Nagaoka Castle had almost fallen,

00:14:37.180 --> 00:14:40.010
but thanks to the brave fighting
of Tsuginosuke Kawai,

00:14:40.150 --> 00:14:42.140
Nagaoka Province was successful in retaking it.

00:14:42.720 --> 00:14:47.050
However, due to the poor coordination
between Aizu and the other provinces,

00:14:47.330 --> 00:14:50.660
it was finding itself on the
verge of collapse once again.

00:14:53.230 --> 00:14:57.130
"But the naval force will play a decisive role
in this war going forward.

00:14:58.240 --> 00:15:03.400
"And only if this Enomoto Fleet arrives in time."
Is that what you're trying to say?

00:15:05.540 --> 00:15:08.810
Is this also according to the script you wrote?

00:15:09.110 --> 00:15:12.080
Including the reunion with that monster.

00:15:13.820 --> 00:15:16.690
Just who are you?

00:15:16.690 --> 00:15:20.920
I'm actually more interested in that
than this war itself.

00:15:21.490 --> 00:15:22.890
Well...

00:15:23.590 --> 00:15:28.770
What type of interest would you have
in a scriptwriter for a traveling troupe?

00:15:28.770 --> 00:15:29.790
Don't you play dumb with me.

00:15:30.270 --> 00:15:37.730
Your true goal is to be the author
of this country and this era.

00:15:38.080 --> 00:15:41.650
That's why you have come to me.

00:15:41.650 --> 00:15:42.670
Am I wrong?

00:15:44.150 --> 00:15:48.550
I'll be looking forward to your script
and the performance.

00:15:55.760 --> 00:15:58.890
Hey, I touched Miss Kaku's hand!

00:15:59.100 --> 00:16:01.000
What? Why?

00:15:59.160 --> 00:16:08.110
TEA

00:15:59.160 --> 00:16:08.110
DUMPLING

00:16:01.030 --> 00:16:03.600
When she gave me the flyer
her hand touched mine!

00:16:03.600 --> 00:16:05.100
That's not fair!

00:16:05.100 --> 00:16:07.300
She's here right now. In Shinagawa.

00:16:07.570 --> 00:16:08.640
Look!

00:16:08.640 --> 00:16:12.740
"The Ghost-Sealing Moontear Assassin"...

00:16:13.480 --> 00:16:16.340
"The Head of the Conqueror versus
The Eternal Assassin"...

00:16:16.880 --> 00:16:18.610
Hmm, it sounds interesting.

00:16:18.680 --> 00:16:21.580
That kind of story is perfect for summer!

00:16:21.790 --> 00:16:22.790
Because it gives you chills?

00:16:22.790 --> 00:16:23.520
Exactly!

00:17:04.500 --> 00:17:07.460
That was pretty good, huh?
The Eternal Assassin!

00:17:08.370 --> 00:17:10.430
I think I should play the role.

00:17:10.430 --> 00:17:12.000
You're just standing in!

00:17:12.000 --> 00:17:16.240
I'm sorry. You can play it only until we get
the rest of the script from the master.

00:17:16.240 --> 00:17:18.110
It's a fantastic role.

00:17:18.110 --> 00:17:19.380
You're just standing in.

00:17:19.380 --> 00:17:21.280
Shut up! I know that!

00:17:22.510 --> 00:17:23.480
Don't get too worked up.

00:17:23.580 --> 00:17:24.840
Stop teasing me!

00:17:25.050 --> 00:17:27.380
Everyone, let's take a quick break!

00:17:27.380 --> 00:17:28.250
Yeah.

00:17:29.050 --> 00:17:31.720
Hey, I'm getting chills.

00:17:32.060 --> 00:17:34.050
I wonder if I caught a cold.

00:17:34.330 --> 00:17:37.690
Actually it's been cold in here for a while now.

00:17:39.560 --> 00:17:40.530
Hey.

00:17:41.200 --> 00:17:42.530
What is this?

00:17:42.530 --> 00:17:43.300
Fog?

00:17:43.300 --> 00:17:44.870
No wonder it's cold.

00:17:44.870 --> 00:17:47.770
But why all of a sudden? What's going on?

00:17:55.180 --> 00:17:56.940
Who are you?

00:17:58.480 --> 00:17:59.350
What is this?

00:17:59.350 --> 00:18:00.680
Monster!

00:18:05.590 --> 00:18:06.890
Let us handle it!

00:18:07.730 --> 00:18:08.730
Leader!

00:18:08.730 --> 00:18:10.590
Follow me outside!

00:18:10.590 --> 00:18:11.200
But!

00:18:11.200 --> 00:18:12.600
You take care of the kids!

00:18:12.600 --> 00:18:13.460
Okay.

00:18:22.470 --> 00:18:23.670
I can't cut it!

00:18:23.670 --> 00:18:25.200
What is this?

00:18:27.610 --> 00:18:28.700
Zagashira!

00:18:31.220 --> 00:18:34.240
Don't tell me... What's going on?

00:18:38.320 --> 00:18:40.590
You two, get out of here!
Go through the back of the stage!

00:18:50.630 --> 00:18:51.600
Kakashi!

00:19:02.350 --> 00:19:03.940
Take the back door! Get outside!

00:19:16.930 --> 00:19:17.990
Leader!

00:19:24.870 --> 00:19:28.070
Leader! Go now!

00:19:28.510 --> 00:19:29.870
Over here! Now!

00:19:34.850 --> 00:19:36.680
No way out anymore...

00:19:37.210 --> 00:19:40.150
They're multiplying...

00:19:44.690 --> 00:19:45.660
Ebisu!

00:19:45.660 --> 00:19:48.350
Damn! What do we do?

00:19:56.900 --> 00:19:57.870
You!

00:19:57.970 --> 00:20:02.300
They're weak against fire!
Go get a torch! Hurry!

00:20:07.010 --> 00:20:09.000
I won't let you lay a finger on her!

00:20:16.190 --> 00:20:18.880
Fire! They're weak against fire!

00:20:30.600 --> 00:20:32.090
Are you guys all right?

00:20:32.500 --> 00:20:36.560
We're all right! That was one tough
rehearsal though.

00:20:38.010 --> 00:20:39.500
Thank goodness!

00:20:39.710 --> 00:20:41.680
What was that about anyway?

00:20:41.880 --> 00:20:44.210
The kids said there were ghosts!

00:20:44.420 --> 00:20:46.850
Once the fog was gone they were gone too.

00:20:47.120 --> 00:20:48.210
Fog?

00:20:48.390 --> 00:20:53.080
Don't worry, Tayu! I killed all of them.

00:20:53.390 --> 00:20:54.550
No.

00:20:55.930 --> 00:20:59.050
Sooner or later they'll appear again.

00:21:03.500 --> 00:21:07.710
Frankly I don't know what the master is thinking.

00:21:07.710 --> 00:21:16.410
But it seems certain that he plans
to grant us our desire this time.

00:21:16.410 --> 00:21:18.810
That's why we've come this far.

00:21:19.220 --> 00:21:24.420
The Kakunojo Yuyama Troupe will perform!
We will perform till the very end!

00:21:24.420 --> 00:21:25.410
Yeah!

00:21:28.330 --> 00:21:34.160
Come one, come all!
We're the Kakunojo Yuyama Troupe!

00:21:46.180 --> 00:21:49.150
Come one, come all!

00:21:58.390 --> 00:22:02.380
<i>THE TROUPE</i>
<i>AT A PROVISIONAL</i>
<i>STAGE AGAIN</i>

00:22:03.560 --> 00:22:09.330
The hand is the sword of love

00:22:09.330 --> 00:22:18.370
It proves the beginning of all

00:22:19.140 --> 00:22:25.100
Beyond the sparkling sky

00:22:25.550 --> 00:22:30.320
The dream is still an illusion

00:22:31.460 --> 00:22:34.560
Running on the path

00:22:34.560 --> 00:22:42.070
Just like chasing the shadow of the moonlight

00:22:42.070 --> 00:22:47.840
The torn sword of love

00:22:47.840 --> 00:23:00.080
At the end of it thousands of teardrops become one

00:23:00.080 --> 00:23:05.890
And brighten tomorrow

00:23:05.890 --> 00:23:11.600
This hand is the sword of love

00:23:11.600 --> 00:23:20.300
It proves the beginning of all

00:23:32.840 --> 00:23:47.600
EPISODE 12
RYOMA'S
MESSAGE

00:23:33.820 --> 00:23:36.750
Sotetsu Ibaragi, where is the Head?

00:23:36.750 --> 00:23:39.690
Akizuki, you're the last person
I'd hand the Head to!

00:23:39.690 --> 00:23:42.260
Well, well, well, look who's here.

00:23:42.260 --> 00:23:45.230
The one is the Eternal Assassin,
who's to seal the ghost,

00:23:45.230 --> 00:23:49.330
and the other is the spy sent by
Queen Victoria of Great Britain.

00:23:47.600 --> 00:24:02.570
RYOMA'S
MESSAGE

00:23:49.530 --> 00:23:54.610
I see, I see. Each of you has your own mission.

00:23:54.770 --> 00:24:01.910
Why don't I write some more
and put an end to the story?
